important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Be Supposed to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + to be + supposed to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">are not supposed to</span> travel on Friday the 13th. <br/>I <span class =\"strong\">was supposed to</span> take a trip on Friday the 13th, but I canceled it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say <span class=\"italic\">be supposed to</span>, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "On Friday the 13th, you are not supposed to cut your hair.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are supposed to stay home on Friday the thirteenth.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I am supposed to move on to another topic.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing-reading-looking).<br/> An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do \u2013 to have \u2013 to speak).<br/><br/> There are verbs you can use with <span class=\"strong\">gerunds</span> and verbs you can use with<span class=\"strong\"> infinitives</span>. <br> Note that the <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> can also be used as the subject of the sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These verbs are commonly followed by a <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span>:<br/><br/>  To express <span class=\"strong\">likes </span>and <span class=\"strong\">dislikes </span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">like*<br/> love*<br/> enjoy<br/> hate*</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:   <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">love reading</span> my fan's questions.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">like</span>/<span class=\"italic\">love</span>/<span class=\"italic\">hate</span> can also be followed by an infinitive.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These are some verbs that are followed by an <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> hope<br/> seem<br/> decide<br/> start</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">hoped to discover</span> something interesting about Friday the 13th.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use<span class=\"strong\"> infinitives</span> after <span class=\"strong\">adjectives</span>. <br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">She is <span class=\"strong\">afraid to talk</span> about Friday the 13th.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An activity can be expressed as a <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span>- this <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> functions as the subject of the sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Reading</span> my fan mail is really interesting.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Writing about the Friday the 13th</span>  was a great idea.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in relation to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the context of; in connection with", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will talk about the superstition this time in relation to Friday the 13th. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about superstitions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to establish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to figure out; determine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have established why 13 is considered an unlucky number.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hypothesize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to form a hypothesis, or to guess based on research", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some writers hypothesize that Jesus was killed on a Friday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bad reputation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a negative belief or opinion that is generally held about someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Another theory claims that Friday got its bad reputation from the book The Canterbury Tales.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "misfortune", "type": "name"}, {"content": "bad luck", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Friday is referred to as a day of  misfortune. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "throughout", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in every part of ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Throughout \"The Canterbury Tales\" Friday is referred to as a day of  misfortune. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bad hair day", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A day on which everything seems to go wrong,", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now that's a bad hair day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss with a group your feelings about Friday the 13th. Is it really a bad luck day? Have you had any bad luck on this day? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Brainstorm with a partner all the things you can and cannot do on Friday the 13th.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use \"supposed to\" and \"not supposed to\" to make your sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research on the Internet all the other dos and don'ts and compare them with yours.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Are there any other superstitious days in your culture and are there things you are supposed to do and not do on those days? ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about manners, customs and superstitions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my attitudes toward an action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I research information to support my opinions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le17ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le17ob02re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn8le17ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn8le17ob02re2img05.jpg", "text": "Our superstition mailbag continues. Today, I'm supposed to move on to another topic, but I decided to spend more time on the number 13, this time in relation to Friday the 13th<br/><br/>We have established why 13 is considered an unlucky number, but why Friday?\nSome writers hypothesize that Jesus was killed on a Friday, making the day unlucky. Another theory claims that Friday got its bad reputation from the book <span class = \"italic\">The Canterbury Tales</span>, where throughout Friday is referred to as a day of  misfortune. Which is true? I have no idea, but I do know some of the things you shouldn't do on Friday the 13th.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn8le17ob02re2img02.jpg", "text": "For example, on Friday the 13th, you're not supposed to travel because you will have bad luck. You are not supposed to cut your hair because if you do, someone in your family will die. Now that's a bad hair day.", "id": 2, "time": "44500"}, {"image": "engenn8le17ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "Finally, being born on Friday the 13th will result in the child being unlucky for life - which for me, is just another reason to blame your parents for everything.\n<br/><br/> I tend to believe that Friday the 13th is just another day. I enjoy talking about it, but I just can't believe that Friday the 13th is an evil day. So if you'll excuse me, I have some mirrors to break and a ladder to walk under.", "id": 3, "time": "59000"}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about my attitudes toward an action. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you believe Friday the 13th is a bad luck day? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"con